     "topic": "Store cleanup order after failure to close an opened listener",
     "kind": "answered_later",
     "quotes": [
      "Nothing is served until every check passed; a listener that cannot be\nopened closes the one already opened and has `store.discard_new_store`\nremove a store this start made new (A17 rule 2); a restart ends every owner\nsession (A13 rule 2). It decides no check."
     ],
     "why": "The later start-operation contract requires listener-open failure to invoke store.discard_new_store, so a failed listener close cannot terminate the process before that store cleanup.",
